      "detail": "[altflow_diverge_points] Alternative flow claim 0 describes Problem Work Order data as editable and exportable to ASCII delimited files but does not identify which existing main_flow step it diverges from. The intended branch point (step 6, export) is not stated in the claim, so the divergence point cannot be verified against main_flow. (atomic grounding: candidate remains incomplete (Explicit evidence that the alternative flow is triggered by the user selecting the Problem Work Order log; the cited cards support edit/export of Problem Work Order data to ASCII delimited files, but not the selection condition.))",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "alternative_flow",
      "detail": "[altflow_diverge_points] The alternative flow attaches to main_flow step 1, but its claim concerns editing/exporting Problem Work Order data as ASCII delimited files. That is logically unrelated to the main-flow step where the Operator initiates display of logs; it would more plausibly diverge at the display/export steps (e.g., step 3, 4, or 6). (atomic grounding: candidate remains incomplete (Explicit source evidence of how this alternative flow resumes or exits after Problem Work Order data entry/export is missing.))",
      "evidence_refs": []
